 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787; this aria was added for the Vienna performances of 1788). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation: \"quell' ira\" printed with the apostrophe word on its own note (two words, kwel + ˈi.ra, as the app's other quell' tokens); \"le incresce\" sung le‿in on one note (libretto \"l'incresce\"); \"quel che a lei\" sung che‿a on one note, except in bar 41 where the print has \"ch'a\" on one syllable; the repeats (\"morte, morte mi dà\", \"e non ho bene, s'ella non l'ha\" three times, the quick restatement of the first four lines from bar 52, and the closing \"morte mi dà\" and \"quel che le incresce\") as printed. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S22) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Don Ottavio sings the first stanza, the middle stanza and the first stanza again. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ; \"lei\" on a single note is ˈlei. Translation literal, for meaning.",
